' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/vo/GetSessionResponseVO.java.
' Observed behavior: JsonProperty currently exposes snake_case response fields.
' Observed behavior: pi exposes phase, reasoning effort, transcript, attached, and locked
' in its protocol snapshot.
' Observed behavior: Anthropic exposes a control-plane Session resource without transcript
' or an active Run recovery snapshot.
' Product constraint: CampusClaw exposes a boolean deep-thinking switch instead of effort levels.
' Architecture change: the confirmed response removes the former public active Run pointer.
' Architecture change: target response fields use lowerCamelCase and do not accept snake_case aliases.
' Architecture change: lifetimeUsage is atomically accumulated in t_session_materialized.
' Design reason: Session state is the coarse control-plane signal; GET Session Events and the
' initiating POST stream own durable recovery and live execution detail.
' Observed behavior: these wire-contract fields exist in GetSessionResponseVO.

left to right direction
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  ArrowColor #475569
  FontColor #0F172A
  AttributeFontColor #0F172A
  StereotypeFontColor #475569
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF7ED
  BorderColor #C2410C
  FontColor #7C2D12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #475569

class GetSessionResult <<target_wire_contract>> {
  +sessionId: session- plus 32 hex UUID characters
  +agentId: string
  +modelId: string
  +createdAt: timestamp
  +updatedAt: timestamp
}

class Usage <<target_wire_contract>> {
  +input: long
  +output: long
  +cacheRead: long
  +cacheWrite: long
  +totalTokens: long
}

class Cost <<usd>> {
  +input: decimal
  +output: decimal
  +cacheRead: decimal
  +cacheWrite: decimal
  +total: decimal
}

enum SessionState {
  idle
  running
}

enum DeepThinkingSwitch {
  false
  true
}

GetSessionResult --> "1" SessionState : state
GetSessionResult --> "1" DeepThinkingSwitch : thinking
GetSessionResult --> "1" Usage : lifetimeUsage
Usage --> "1" Cost : cost

note bottom of GetSessionResult
This is the confirmed public Session resource.
State is idle or running and carries no execution identity.
GET Session Events cursors and live progress belong to other operations.
end note
@enduml

@startuml http_delete_session
title CampusClaw HTTP Session Logical Deletion Confirmed Design

' Source evidence (pi-mono 5cd93f688aaab89dbb6dfa4aca535f21796ae185):
' packages/coding-agent/src/core/agent-session.ts, AgentSession.dispose, lines 789-805
' packages/coding-agent/src/modes/interactive/components/session-selector.ts,
' deleteSessionFile, lines 598-630
' Source evidence (pi-mono-java PR 167 f60cc3e78bb8b700527ac082c7c8e10524ede095):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/session/RuntimeSessionService.java, delete.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository.java, beginDeletion.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/session/SessionCleanupWorker.java.
' Source evidence (pi-mono-java PR 167 f60cc3e78bb8b700527ac082c7c8e10524ede095):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeSessionController.java, delete.
' Observed behavior: the current Java delete path still names the variable session_id.
' Observed behavior: pi dispose stops active work and releases runtime resources, while
' interactive deletion removes the local JSONL file.
' Observed behavior: the implemented repository returns BUSY for a running session and does not abort it.
' Observed behavior: tombstone insertion, cleanup task insertion, and session deletion commit atomically.
' Architecture change: logical deletion and a durable cleanup work item replace local JSONL deletion.
' Architecture change: the target HTTP path variable is sessionId; database column names remain snake_case.
' Product constraint: all Runtime operations carry integration-context headers without local validation.
' Design reason: the API becomes idempotent immediately without exposing cleanup-job state.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #475569
  ActorBorderColor #475569
  ActorFontColor #0F172A
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantBorderColor #475569
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
  GroupBorderColor #64748B
  GroupFontColor #334155
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF7ED
  BorderColor #C2410C
  FontColor #7C2D12
}

actor Caller
participant "DeleteSession\nAPI" as API
database "Runtime Session\nStore" as Store
participant "Cleanup\nWorker" as Worker

Caller -> API : DELETE /sessions/{sessionId}\ncontext headers and no body
API -> API : do not validate integration credentials
API -> API : validate sessionId
API -> Store : beginLogicalDelete(sessionId)

alt existing idle Session
  Store -> Store : transaction: insert tombstone, enqueue cleanup,\ndelete session row
  Store --> API : DELETED
  API --> Caller : 204 No Content
  Worker -> Store : claim cleanup work item
  Worker -> Store : complete remaining cleanup
  Worker -> Store : complete and delete cleanup work item
else existing running Session
  Store --> API : BUSY
  API --> Caller : 409 SESSION_BUSY\nResultBean error without result
else missing or deleted
  Store --> API : NOT_FOUND
  API --> Caller : 204 No Content
else atomic commit failed
  Store --> API : failure, no partial deletion
  API --> Caller : 500 SESSION_DELETE_FAILED\nResultBean error without result
end

note over API,Store
Logical deletion is complete at 204.
Physical cleanup remains retryable and internal.
end note

note over Store,Worker
mate-service Chat metadata and file objects
are outside this operation boundary.
end note

note right of Store
The permanent tombstone has exactly two fields:
session_id and deleted_at.
Cleanup state, retries, errors, and owner data stay out.
end note
@enduml
